y":0.08688059470086613,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":89.5,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.0026278031141900304,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":96.7,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.0070457348023851285,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":37.2,"_gate_rev_durability":0.11509343079424972,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":82.5,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.024572658819251428,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":38.4,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.004328131591521345,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":55.4,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.011480148566628509,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":80.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.027590001,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":18.4,"_gate_insider_buying":0.042,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":4.2,"pf":[],"description_full":"Farmers & Merchants Bancorp, Inc. operates as the bank holding company for The Farmers & Merchants State Bank that provides commercial banking services to individuals and small businesses in Northwest Ohio, Northeast Indiana, and Southeast Michigan. The company offers checking, savings, and time deposit accounts; certificates of deposit; and custodial services for individual retirement and health savings accounts. It also provides commercial, agricultural, and residential mortgage, as well as consumer lending products; loans for farmland, farm equipment, and livestock; operating loans for seeds, fertilizers, and feeds; home improvement loans; and loans for autos, trucks, recreational vehicles, and motorcycles. In addition, the company offers commercial real estate loans, such as lines of credit and machinery purchase loans. Further, it provides automated teller machine or interactive teller machine services; and online and mobile banking, bill-pay, on-line statement opportunities, and remote deposit capture or electronic deposit processing. Additionally, the company offers electronic transaction origination, such as wire and automated clearing house file transmittal services. Farmers & Merchants Bancorp, Inc. was founded in 1897 and is headquartered in Archbold, Ohio.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Lars B. Eller | President, CEO & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $842,691 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 486 people. Revenue per employee of $250K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 9%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $72K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Farmers & Merchants Bancorp, In is a small-cap financial services business with a $507M market cap on $121M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $35M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 29 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.10\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.5% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 2.8% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.3428447903156088},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (96% sell ratio, net $2.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 39% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","20 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(FMAO) Movement Within Algorithmic Entry Frameworks","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/16/FMAO_Movement_Within_Algorithmic_Entry_Frameworks_111126073801_1794400681.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794400681.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Farmers & Merchants Bancorp (NASDAQ:FMAO) Stock Purchase Reported by Rep. Robert E. Latta","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/farmers-merchants-bancorp-nasdaqfmao-stock-purchase-reported-by-rep-robert-e-latta.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793948471.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Price-Driven Insight from (FMAO) for Rule-Based Strategy","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/21/Price-Driven_Insight_from_FMAO_for_Rule-Based_Strategy_110126074001_1793536801.html","date":"2026-11-01","timestamp":1793536801.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Farmers & Merchants Bancorp (NASDAQ:FMAO) Stock Lifted to \u201cStrong-Buy\u201d by Zacks Research","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/30/farmers-merchants-bancorp-nasdaqfmao-stock-lifted-to-strong-buy-by-zacks-research.html","date":"2026-10-30","timestamp":1793361666.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.477,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Farmers & Merchants Bancorp (NASDAQ:FMAO) Posts Earnings Results","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/22/farmers-merchants-bancorp-nasdaqfmao-posts-earnings-results.html","date":"2026-10-22","timestamp":1792707165.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Critical Comparison: Bank of America (NYSE:BAC) versus Farmers & Merchants 